    "updated_at": "2026-11-25T03:56:33Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/3662-camtools-rest · PR #3965 · pinned by a_neck_that_meets_the_flank_exactly_is_accepted, an_unstated_range_reads_as_the_one_stated_pitch, a_catalog_single_form_thread_mill_without_a_range_cuts_its_one_pitch, converted_3662::a_single_form_thread_mill_without_a_pitch_range_loads, converted_3662::the_3662_form_mill_rides_the_file_as_a_necked_single_form_thread_mill, converted_3662::the_3662_tapered_mills_round_trip_with_their_tips · merges at the next cut\n\nCovered and remaining:\n- Tapered mill with a flat tip or a ball tip: covered on main by PR #3929 (`.camtools` version 6). This PR pins the synthetic numbers of this issue.\n- Drawn cutter outline in `.camtools`: covered on main by PR #3906 (version 5).\n- Form mill with a drawn profile: covered on main by PR #3946, for outlines whose radius does not narrow upward.\n- The synthetic form mill of this issue (one V tooth on a neck): carried as a single-form thread mill with its drawn cutter (this PR).\n- Single-form thread mill without a pitch range: this PR. A definition without the `pitch_min` key reads as a range of its one pitch. The operation cuts only that pitch. No version step: the writer is unchanged.\n- Dovetail neck tolerance: this PR, 1e-9 mm.\n- Remaining: a general form mill whose outline narrows upward stays with #896. Operations that cut with a flat-tip or ball-tip taper are outside this issue; they refuse such a tool by name.\n\nI cannot set labels. A collaborator, please replace `claimed` with `in-review`.",
